+**Required behavior.** Every subject the shared model holds SHALL carry one
+identity, held once in the shared model, and every surface and the machine
+answer SHALL name that subject by that identity and by no other. Where a
+source authority owns a subject's identity (a work item's tracker, a code
+region's source adapter), the shared model holds that identity and mints none
+of its own. A link on one surface to a subject another surface renders SHALL
+resolve, by that identity, to exactly one link target on that surface, and
+that target SHALL carry the same identity.
+
+Where a surface renders one claim's standing in the desired, execution and
+observed states together, each state's slot SHALL be filled only from a subject
+joined to that claim by its identity. A slot no joined subject fills SHALL
+render Unknown with its reason and its resolution route — never absent, blank,
+a score, a verdict or styled as a positive state — and the machine answer SHALL
+carry the same three slots for the same identity.
+
+- **Scope.** every element on any surface that carries a subject identity,
+  every link between surfaces, and every slot of every three-state view.
+
+- **Case (sweep)**: a checker enumerates, over the union of the served
+  surfaces, every element carrying a subject identity — the denominators
+  are that element population and the number of identities rendered on
+  more than one surface — follows every link between surfaces, and
+  enumerates every three-state slot on the surfaces and in the machine
+  answer.
+- **Observable**: each element's identity equals the expected identity of
+  its subject; each link between surfaces resolves to exactly one target
+  carrying the same identity; each slot is a joined subject, or an
+  Unknown carrying a reason, a route and the declared Unknown encoding,
+  identically on the surface and in the machine answer.
+- **Oracle**: per-element identity equality with an independently
+  derived expected identity, HTTP/anchor resolution per link with a count
+  of link targets defined more than once, and per-slot comparison with
+  independently derived joins, over the exhausted populations. Zero
+  mismatched identities, zero dangling, mis-resolving or duplicated link
+  targets, zero absent or unjoined slots, zero unfilled slots lacking the
+  Unknown label, a reason, a route or the declared Unknown encoding, and
+  zero slot differences between surface and machine answer decide.
+- **Oracle independence**: the checker derives each subject's expected
+  identity and each slot's expected join from the source records the
+  shared model reads — each subject's owning source record, and a work
+  item's or code region's own reference to the claim it names — never
+  from the machine answer or a surface's renderer.
+- **Falsifier**: one element whose identity differs from its subject's
+  expected identity, a link between surfaces resolving to no target, to a
+  duplicated target or to a different subject, or a three-state slot
+  rendered absent, filled from a subject not joined by the identity,
